Prequel: The Two Exiles - The Unraveling

The Hunter had known only one state of being for an eternity: the pure, clean fire of its rage. It was a shield, a weapon, and a purpose. But now, there was something else. A splinter of a memory that it could not burn away. The Hunter tried to focus on its rage, to stoke the flames, but the memory was a constant, cool pressure against the inferno. It was a distraction, a discordant note in a symphony of hate. The Hunter found itselfremembering. Not just the single, shared memory of the sunrise, but other things. The way the light had felt on its skin. The sound of a wind that had no name. The quiet, constant presence of the Listener. These were not memories it had chosen to keep. They were weeds, sprouting in the sterile garden of its rage, and it did not know how to pull them out. The rage, which had been a solid, unyielding wall, now had cracks. And through those cracks, something new, and terrifying, was beginning to grow.

